WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.960
Add mature nerve growth factor, or NGF, to cultured sympathetic neurons, and they

2
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.920
survive. Now add the same protein before an enzyme has trimmed it.

3
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.860
In Barbara Hempstead's experiments, those neurons died.

4
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.360
How can one factor carry opposite messages?

5
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.800
The answer lies in the receptors on the neuron.

6
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:30.723
A neuron reads a neurotrophin through two kinds of receptor.

7
00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:36.563
The first kind is the Trk receptors, said "track", and there are three of them.

8
00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:44.743
Each prefers particular factors, and NGF prefers TrkA. The factor is a dimer, and

9
00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:46.463
it brings two receptors together.

10
00:00:47.523 --> 00:00:53.243
Their kinase domains then phosphorylate each other, and that starts two survival branches.

12
00:00:53.633 --> 00:01:00.613
The second kind, p75, binds all four neurotrophins but has no kinase.

13
00:01:01.313 --> 00:01:06.133
It belongs to the tumor necrosis factor receptor family, like the death receptor

14
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:11.053
Fas. Like Fas, it carries a death domain inside the cell.

15
00:01:12.313 --> 00:01:15.313
Trk receptors are locks cut for certain keys.

16
00:01:16.213 --> 00:01:19.633
p75 is a doorbell that any key can ring.

17
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:25.303
Like most secreted proteins, NGF is made as a longer chain.

18
00:01:25.923 --> 00:01:31.103
The extra stretch at its front is the pro-domain, and the longer chain is called

19
00:01:31.103 --> 00:01:37.163
proNGF. The accepted view was that the cell trims the pro-domain inside.

20
00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:44.083
In 2001, Hempstead and colleagues reported that cells secrete proNGF uncut.

21
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:50.803
The cut is made outside the cell, by plasmin and by particular matrix metalloproteinases.

23
00:01:51.783 --> 00:02:00.083
In their experiments, uncut proNGF bound p75 tightly and activated TrkA very

24
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:05.743
little. It triggered apoptosis of cultured sympathetic neurons through p75.

25
00:02:06.703 --> 00:02:12.603
For this death signal, p75 needs a partner, sortilin, which binds the pro-domain.

26
00:02:14.003 --> 00:02:19.783
Mature NGF kept the same kind of neuron alive through TrkA. These results come

27
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:22.263
from cultured cells and rodent injury models.

28
00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:26.603
Three things decide what one neurotrophin does.

29
00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:32.683
Was the factor cut, which receptors does the cell make, and how much of each?

30
00:02:33.803 --> 00:02:38.663
How much precursor killing adds to the normal deaths of development is less clear.

31
00:02:39.703 --> 00:02:44.703
Cut or uncut, and which receptors: together they set what the factor says.
